N5008 [temp.deduct.type]/8: a form mismatch (P=tuple<_Elements...>& vs
A=int*) fails the ENTIRE deduction; the pack must not be resurrected as
empty.  The nil-poisoned pack argument is now tagged #deduction_failed and
the candidate rejected.  Distilled from libstdc++'s constrained tuple-swap
overload probed by _Node_handle::swap's `using std::swap;` two-step, whose
empty-pack resurrection collaterally instantiated swap<void> (void __tmp
aborting the enclosing conversion -- the map emplace chain).
g++/clang++ runtime-verified.
